        "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelumbo_nucifera",
        "description": "Nelumbo nucifera, also known as Padma (Sanskrit: \\u092a\\u0926\\u094d\\u092e, romanized: Padm\\u0101, lit.\\u2009'Lotus') or Kamala (Sanskrit: \\u0915\\u092e\\u0932, lit. 'Lotus'), sacred lotus, pink lotus, Indian lotus, or simply lotus, is one of two extant species of aquatic plant in the family Nelumbonaceae. It is sometimes colloquially called a water lily, though this more often refers to members of the family Nymphaeaceae. The lotus belongs in the order Proteales."
